# Rule catalog

This folder is the **editable catalog** for your personal always-on rules. After changes here, sync to `~/.cursor/rules/` (see `source-of-truth.mdc`).

| Rule file | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `source-of-truth.mdc` | Where rules and skills live; sync workflow |
| `persistent-proactive-developer.mdc` | Finish work, no mocks, real integrations, proactive next steps |
| `incremental-delivery.mdc` | One user story at a time until DoD |
| `dod.mdc` | Completion checklist before marking done |
| `common-test-strategy.mdc` | Test pyramid, TDD, quality checklist (baseline for DoD “Quality met”) |
| `makefile.mdc` | `dev` / `up` / `down` on new projects |
| `i18n-support.mdc` | Key-based copy across req → design → impl → test |
| `writing-style.mdc` | Tone, structure, and language for replies and docs |

## Precedence

1. **Stricter wins** when two rules overlap (e.g. DoD vs common test strategy).
2. **DoD** is the gate for “done”; it references **common-test-strategy** for quality, **incremental-delivery** for scope, and **retrospective** (skill) for persistence.
3. **Do not** maintain a separate `test-strategy.mdc` — it duplicates **common-test-strategy** and causes conflicting guidance.

## Skills often used with these rules

- `retrospective` — DoD retrospective section
- `new-requirement` — scope discovered mid-story (`incremental-delivery`, `persistent-proactive-developer`)
- `tdd` / project test strategy — extends **common-test-strategy**, never weakens it
